Fail when several sources are given and DEST is not a directory.
"install a b c" with a c that is not a directory copied each source to
c in turn, so only the last remained and no error was reported. Check,
as coreutils does, that DEST is a directory when there is more than one
source, before copying anything.

---
 coreutils/install.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/coreutils/install.c
+++ b/coreutils/install.c
@@ -193,6 +193,8 @@
 		argv[argc] = NULL;
 		/* coreutils install resolves link in this case, don't use lstat */
 		isdir = stat(last, &statbuf) < 0 ? 0 : S_ISDIR(statbuf.st_mode);
+		if (argc > 1 && !isdir)
+			bb_error_msg_and_die("target '%s' is not a directory", last);
 	}
 
 	if (argc < 1)
